                        "entry_id": "63999d2b-add0-3eae-8e89-61fed580cf5f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The fruit of the wax myrtle shrub; or the plant itself (Morella cerifera), with aromatic, leathery leaves and waxy berries."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Canada",
                            "US"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4a079386-b16b-455a-af34-eab243015f84",
                                "sense_id": "5c4cfcc6-f6b9-30d6-ad6d-8494d86b5c90",
                                "text": "It twisted and turned, and, the first thing I knew, made a sudden bend around a bunch of bayberry scrub and opened out into a big clear space like a lawn."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1295dbd9-c34a-379f-b7ce-0f32b5388b78",
                        "entry_id": "63999d2b-add0-3eae-8e89-61fed580cf5f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The fruit of the wax myrtle shrub; or the plant itself (Morella cerifera), with aromatic, leathery leaves and waxy berries.",
                            "Other species in the family Myricaceae, especially in genus Myrica; bay-rum tree, candleberry."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Canada",
                            "US"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "de1654d8-2cc2-4b04-9673-76827e869e11",
                                "sense_id": "1295dbd9-c34a-379f-b7ce-0f32b5388b78",
                                "text": "The two North American genera are Myrica (bayberry) and Comptonia (sweet-fern)."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "359f0914-a174-3bc2-bbe6-395ee1678b77",
                        "entry_id": "63999d2b-add0-3eae-8e89-61fed580cf5f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The fruit of the bay laurel (Laurus nobilis)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d9ee43da-614f-4e5c-8924-ecb790f902d1",
                                "sense_id": "359f0914-a174-3bc2-bbe6-395ee1678b77",
                                "text": "[T]heir shape was much like a Figg, but very much smaller, some being about the bigness of a Bay-berry, others, and the biggest, of a Hazel-Nut."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
